      Taurus:      `Taurus governing your 3rd house grants Venus's aesthetic refinement to your communication style, making you a naturally gifted writer, artist, musician, or orator with a feel for beauty in language. Your siblings or close companions likely share a love of comfort, creativity, or financial acumen. Short journeys tend toward pleasurable, culturally enriching destinations rather than purely practical trips. Your hands possess artistic skill — craft, music, or design may be your most natural expressive medium.`,
      Gemini:      `Gemini in your 3rd house, with Mercury as lord, creates an exceptionally powerful placement for communication, intellect, and all forms of media. Your mind moves with extraordinary speed between topics, and your ability to explain complex ideas simply gives you a remarkable advantage in writing, journalism, teaching, and trade. The sibling dynamic in your life is characterised by mental stimulation, debate, and shared curiosity. Short travels are frequent and mentally enriching, often turning into unexpected sources of information and connection.`,
      Cancer:      `Cancer ruling your 3rd house gives the Moon sovereignty over your Parakrama Bhava, infusing your courage and communication with emotional sensitivity and intuitive insight. Your bravery tends to be protective in nature — you are most courageous when defending those you love. Siblings and close companions carry a nurturing, emotionally complex quality in your life. Short journeys often connect you to water, family roots, or emotionally significant places that quietly shape your worldview.`,
      Leo:         `Leo in your 3rd house places the Sun at the helm of your Parakrama Bhava, giving your communication a natural authority and dramatic flair. You speak and write with confidence that commands attention, and creative self-expression through performance, leadership, or public speaking comes naturally to you. Siblings may be prominent figures in their own right, or the sibling dynamic carries a competitive, pride-oriented quality. Your courage is solar — bright, visible, and oriented toward earning recognition for bold action.`,
      Virgo:       `Virgo governing your 3rd house makes Mercury the lord of Parakrama in its most analytical manifestation — you communicate with precision, write with craftsmanlike care, and approach every initiative with a methodical plan. Your courage is quiet but persistent; you overcome obstacles through preparation rather than brute force. Siblings may be practically oriented, health-conscious, or involved in skilled trades. Short journeys often serve practical purposes — training, research, and professional networking.`,
      Libra:       `Libra in your 3rd house places Venus as lord of Parakrama, lending a diplomatic, partnership-oriented quality to your initiatives and communications. You are most effective when you collaborate — your courage finds its fullest expression in joint ventures and creative partnerships rather than solitary pioneering. Siblings or close companions tend to be charming, relationship-oriented individuals who reflect Venusian values back to you. Short journeys often involve cultural, artistic, or social events that expand your network.`,
      Scorpio:     `Scorpio ruling your 3rd house gives Mars a secretive, investigative quality over your courage and communication. You do not reveal your strategies in advance — your boldness operates below the surface, and you are far more formidable than you initially appear. Siblings or close companions may carry an intense, transformative presence in your life. Your writing and speech can be penetratingly powerful, making you well-suited to investigative journalism, psychological counselling, occult writing, or strategic planning.`,
      Sagittarius: `Sagittarius in your 3rd house gives Jupiter a philosophical, expansive quality over your Parakrama Bhava — you are courageous in the realm of ideas, willing to champion unpopular truths and speak wisdom where others would remain silent. Your communication is broad, visionary, and infused with a natural teaching quality. Siblings or close companions often serve as philosophical companions or gurus in your journey. Short journeys frequently expand into longer voyages of discovery, blurring the boundary between the 3rd and 9th houses.`,
